ryName","quote":"raw.githubusercontent.com","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1685.005","name":"Clear Windows Event Logs","parent":"Disable or Modify Tools","tactics":["Defense Impairment"],"behavior":"PowerShell and spawned processes accessed HKLM\\SYSTEM\\ControlSet001\\Control\\Lsa registry key and Internet Settings cache, while the System event log was cleared.","slot":2,"reasoning":"The primary adversary objective is clearing the System event log to hide intrusion activity, which is the most specific and direct behavior evidenced. While the LSA registry access could suggest persistence or credential dumping, the clearing of event logs is the defining action that demonstrates defense impairment and log tampering.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E001","field":"Channel","quote":"System","ok":true},{"event_id":"E012","field":"ObjectName","quote":"\\REGISTRY\\MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\ControlSet001\\Control\\Lsa","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1059.003","name":"Windows Command Shell","parent":"Command and Scripting Interpreter","tactics":["Execution"],"behavior":"hh.exe spawned cmd.exe which executed calc.exe, establishing a process execution chain with full access rights between processes.","slot":1,"reasoning":"The operator used hh.exe (Help and Support) to spawn cmd.exe, which then executed calc.exe via command-line invocation. This is command shell execution for running a program, not a persistence mechanism or privilege escalation. The full access rights between processes reflect normal parent-child relationships, not hijacking or exploitation.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E023","field":"CommandLine","quote":"\"C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe\" /c calc.exe","ok":true},{"event_id":"E024","field":"ParentImage","quote":"C:\\Windows\\hh.exe","ok":true},{"event_id":"E030","field":"ParentProcessName","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe","ok":true}],"attempts":1}],"unverified":[],"declined":[],"hypotheses":[{"behavior":"PowerShell downloaded a compiled HTML help file from GitHub (raw.githubusercontent.com) and executed it via hh.exe to achieve code execution.","event_ids":["E002","E003","E004","E005","E006","E007"],"keywords":["CHM","hh.exe","T1218.001","compiled HTML help","GitHub","code execution"]},{"behavior":"hh.exe spawned cmd.exe which executed calc.exe, establishing a process execution chain with full access rights between processes.","event_ids":["E023","E024","E028","E030","E031"],"keywords":["process creation","cmd.exe","calc.exe","process access","execution"]},{"behavior":"PowerShell and spawned processes accessed HKLM\\SYSTEM\\ControlSet001\\Control\\Lsa registry key and Internet Settings cache, while the System event log was cleared.","event_ids":["E001","E012","E013","E020","E021"],"keywords":["registry access","LSA","event log clearing","anti-forensics","Internet Settings"]}],"retried":[]},"trace":[{"t":1.83,"agent":"hunter","kind":"text","text":"I'll analyze this recording to identify the adversary behaviors. Let me start by examining the events and searching for additional context."},{"t":1.84,"agent":"hunter","kind":"tool_result","tool":"search_events","result":{"matches":3,"events":"<log_events trust=\"untrusted\">\n[E002] +4s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 11 file created: Image=C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe TargetFilename=C:\\ProgramData\\T1218.001.chm\n[E006] +5s WORKSTATION5 Security 4688 process created: SubjectUserName=wardog ParentProcessName=C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe NewProcessName=C:\\Windows\\hh.exe CommandLine=\"\"C:\\windows\\hh.exe\" C:\\ProgramData\\T1218.001.chm\"\n[E007] +5s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 1 process created: User=WORKSTATION5\\wardog IntegrityLevel=High ParentImage=C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe Image=C:\\Windows\\hh.exe CommandLine=\"\"C:\\windows\\hh.exe\" C:\\ProgramData\\T1218.001.chm\"\n</log_events>"}},{"t":9.7,"agent":"hunter","kind":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture of the adversary behaviors. Let me analyze the key findings:\n\n**Key Observations:**\n\n1. **Event Log Clearing (E001)**: System event log was cleared immediately - anti-forensics\n2. **PowerShell Download & Execution (E002-E007)**: PowerShell created a CHM file (T1218.001 - Compiled HTML Help) and executed it via hh.exe\n3. **C2 Communication (E003-E005)**: PowerShell queried github.com and raw.githubusercontent.com, then connected to 140.82.112.4:443 (GitHub IP)\n4. **Living off the Land (E006-E024)**: hh.exe spawned cmd.exe which ran calc.exe - this is a code execution chain\n5. **Registry Manipulation (E012-E022)**: Multiple processes accessed LSA registry and Internet Settings cache\n6. **Process Injection/Access (E009, E028, E032)**: PowerShell and cmd.exe accessed other processes with full access rights\n\nThe primary behaviors are:\n1. **Compiled HTML Help (CHM) abuse** - T1218.001 technique to execute code\n2. **C2 communication** - downloading from GitHub\n3. **Code execution** - spawning calc.exe through cmd.exe"},{"t":9.7,"agent":"hunter","kind":"tool_result","tool":"set_model_response","result":{"assessment":"PowerShell downloaded a malicious CHM file from GitHub and executed it via hh.exe, which then spawned cmd.exe to run calc.exe. The system event log was cleared to cover tracks, and multiple processes accessed sensitive registry keys including LSA settings.","hypotheses":[{"behavior":"PowerShell downloaded a compiled HTML help file from GitHub (raw.githubusercontent.com) and executed it via hh.exe to achieve code execution.","event_ids":["E002","E003","E004","E005","E006","E007"],"keywords":["CHM","hh.exe","T1218.001","compiled HTML help","GitHub","code execution"]},{"behavior":"hh.exe spawned cmd.exe which executed calc.exe, establishing a process execution chain with full access rights between processes.","event_ids":["E023","E024","E028","E030","E031"],"keywords":["process creation","cmd.exe","calc.exe","process access","execution"]},{"behavior":"PowerSh